"Licensed Work" means the original software, source code, documentation, configuration, data, artwork, scenario content, or other material distributed by the Licensor with this license, but only to the extent the Licensor owns the applicable rights.

"Licensor" means AnlionGamer or another copyright holder expressly identified with the Licensed Work.

"Modified Work" means a version of the Licensed Work that has been changed, adapted, translated, extended, or combined with other material in a way that creates a derivative work under applicable law.

"Distribution" means providing a copy of the Licensed Work or a Modified Work to another person.

"Commercial Distribution" means Distribution in exchange for money, a required donation, subscription, purchase, fee, paid membership, paid entitlement, or other consideration, or Distribution as a bundled component of a product whose access requires payment.

2. Ownership

The Licensed Work remains the property of its copyright holder. This license grants permissions to use the Licensed Work; it does not transfer ownership.

No rights are granted to CastleMiner Z, its trademarks, game assets, or any other third-party material except to the extent a separate license from the applicable rights holder permits such use.

3. Permission to Use, Study, and Modify

Subject to this license, you may:

- download, install, run, and use the Licensed Work;
- inspect and study its source code and behavior;
- make backup and archival copies;
- modify the Licensed Work for personal or community use;
- compile or build Modified Works;
- create derivative works based on the Licensed Work; and
- perform legitimate interoperability, compatibility, accessibility, debugging, preservation, and good-faith security work.

4. Permission for Free Distribution

You may distribute the Licensed Work or a Modified Work without charge if all of the following conditions are met:

- the Distribution is not Commercial Distribution;
- this license and the applicable copyright notice are included with the distributed copy;
- existing attribution and third-party notices are preserved;
- a Modified Work is clearly identified as modified and is not represented as an original release by the Licensor;
- the original project name, author, publisher, icons, or presentation are not used deceptively to imply that a fork or modified release was published, approved, or endorsed by the Licensor; and
- the Distribution does not falsely imply affiliation with, sponsorship by, or endorsement from the developers, publisher, or rights holders of CastleMiner Z.

A Modified Work may use a different name and branding. Truthful compatibility statements such as "based on," "forked from," "compatible with," or "requires" are permitted when they do not imply endorsement.

5. No Sale or Paid Access

Without separate written permission from the Licensor, you may not:

- sell, rent, license for a fee, or commercially distribute the Licensed Work;
- sell or commercially distribute a Modified Work that contains or derives from substantial portions of the Licensed Work;
- charge for downloads, access, activation, keys, installers, builds, updates, or early access to the Licensed Work or a Modified Work;
- place the Licensed Work or a Modified Work behind a subscription, paid membership, purchase requirement, or other paywall;
- bundle the Licensed Work or a Modified Work into a paid software package, paid mod pack, paid marketplace listing, or other product whose access requires payment; or
- sublicense the Licensed Work for payment.

Voluntary donations are permitted when they do not purchase, prioritize, unlock, or otherwise condition access to the Licensed Work or a Modified Work.

Videos, livestreams, reviews, tutorials, articles, screenshots, guides, and similar commentary or demonstration may be monetized, provided the Licensed Work itself is not sold or placed behind paid access.

6. Independent Works and Extensions

This license does not claim ownership of independently created work merely because it interoperates with, depends on, or is compatible with the Licensed Work.

An author of an independently created mod, tool, scenario, theme, translation, integration, or other extension retains ownership of that author's original material and may choose separate terms for it, subject to third-party rights.

This section does not permit copying substantial portions of the Licensed Work into another product and treating the copied material as independently created.

7. Responsible Use and Prohibited Malicious Conduct

The Licensed Work may be used for ordinary gameplay modification, single-player experimentation, accessibility, host customization, private or consensual multiplayer modification, debugging, interoperability, and other good-faith purposes.

You may not use the Licensed Work or a Modified Work with the intent to maliciously, deceptively, or non-consensually harm another person, system, host, account, save, world, or multiplayer session.

Prohibited conduct includes intentionally using the Licensed Work or a Modified Work to:

- crash another player's game or multiplayer host;
- corrupt, destroy, or maliciously alter another person's save data, world data, files, or configuration;
- send deliberately malformed or malicious multiplayer or network data to another user or host;
- exploit a vulnerability against a system, account, player, host, or service without authorization;
- gain unauthorized access to another person's computer, account, files, credentials, or game session;
- distribute malware, spyware, credential-stealing code, destructive payloads, or similar malicious software;
- impersonate another player, developer, publisher, service, authority, or the Licensor;
- evade bans, removals, access restrictions, or moderation controls for the purpose of continuing unwanted or abusive activity; or
- deliberately disrupt multiplayer sessions involving people who have not consented to the behavior.

Gameplay changes are not prohibited merely because they alter balance, difficulty, progression, camera behavior, player abilities, items, enemies, or other game mechanics.

8. Good-Faith Security Research

Good-faith security, stability, compatibility, and interoperability research is permitted when performed on systems you own, accounts you control, isolated test environments, or systems for which you have explicit authorization to test.

Research must not intentionally harm uninvolved users, disrupt public multiplayer sessions, obtain unauthorized information, or weaponize vulnerabilities against other people.

